<h2 id="h-built-for-ethical-big-game-hunting">Built for Ethical Big-Game Hunting</h2>
<p>Ethical hunting comes down to placing a sharp broadhead in the vitals with enough energy to pass through. The Bear Alaskan XT gives you the tools for both. The higher draw weight option pairs well with heavier arrows for penetration, and the forgiving brace height helps keep arrows where you aim when your heart is pounding.</p>
<p>For elk and other large animals, many hunters pair the 55&ndash;70 lb version with a heavier arrow and a durable fixed-blade or hybrid broadhead. For deer, either range works well. Whatever you choose, practice with the exact arrow and broadhead you will hunt with, and confirm that broadheads group with field points before the season.</p>

<h2 id="h-riser-construction-and-durability">Riser Construction and Durability</h2>
<p>The Alaskan XT is built around a rigid riser designed to handle hunting abuse: bumps against tree bark, cold mornings, truck rides and the occasional drop. A stiff riser also helps the bow return to the same position on every shot, which matters more for accuracy than most people realize.</p>
<p>At 3.5 pounds bare, the bow stays light without feeling flimsy. Add the RTH accessories and it naturally gets heavier, but it still carries comfortably. A good bow sling makes long hikes even easier and frees your hands for glassing and climbing.</p>

