<h2 id="h-position-within-the-bear-archery-lineup">Bear Alaskan XT vs Species XT RTH and Other Bear Bows</h2>
<p>Bear sells several ready-to-hunt compound bows, and shoppers often compare the Alaskan XT with the <strong>Species XT RTH</strong>. Both are Bear RTH packages aimed at hunters who want a complete setup without building one piece by piece. The Species line is usually positioned as an approachable all-around option, while the Alaskan XT leans toward a longer, steadier frame with a forgiving brace height for big-game hunting. If you are deciding between the Bear Species XT RTH and the Alaskan XT, hold both if you can and compare how they feel at full draw, then check current specs on each.</p>
