<h2 id="h-maintenance-and-long-term-use">Maintenance and Long-Term Use</h2>
<p>A ready-to-hunt bow still needs regular care. Keep these habits and your Alaskan XT will stay accurate for years:</p>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Wax the string and cables</strong> every few weeks of shooting, and more often in dry or dusty conditions.</li>
  <li><strong>Check screws</strong> on the sight, rest, quiver and stabilizer before each hunt. Vibration loosens them over time.</li>
  <li><strong>Inspect the string</strong> for fraying, separated strands or a peep that has rotated.</li>
  <li><strong>Never dry-fire.</strong> Shooting without an arrow can damage the cams, limbs and string.</li>
  <li><strong>Store it in a case</strong>, away from heat. A padded <?= amz('compound bow case', 'compound bow case') ?> protects the sight and cams in the truck.</li>
</ol>
<p>Plan on new strings and cables every couple of seasons depending on how much you shoot, and let a pro shop check cam timing at the same time.</p>

